{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"97a1808b-3908-44a0-8ad6-76ef3f08eadb","status":"SUCCESS","response":"AUDIT-agy-coder-fallback-plan-v1-BEGIN\n## Summary\nPlan v1.6 is aligned only through Spec v1.7 (`c117a695`) and has not incorporated the build-affecting changes from Spec v1.8, v1.9 (`D-15`), and v1.10 (`D-16`), leaving out the fifth FR-1 state field (`implementation_authors` and `AC-1.3`), the `implementation_authors`-backed FR-7 attribution rules and four of the five `AC-7.3` fixtures, the FR-4/FR-6 `unknown`-scan, `kind=`-on-every-deny, empty-path-key, and directory-target (`D-16`) rules in `AC-4.1`/`AC-4.2`, and the `--self-check` exit-0 discipline in FR-5/`AC-5.2`. In addition, Stage 5 directly contradicts Spec FR-5 and `AC-5.2` by stating that `AGY-GATE: UNREADABLE` exits `1` from the check instead of `2`, and §\"Success Criteria\" drops `AC-1.3`, `AC-7.3`, and `AC-9.4` from the automated-test gate list.\n\n## Must-fix\n- Plan v1.6 omits the fifth FR-1 state field `implementation_authors` and `AC-1.3` added in Spec v1.9 (`D-15`) — Spec FR-1 declares five optional fields (`implementer`, `agy_status`, `implementer_switch`, `review_independence`, and `implementation_authors`) and pins `implementation_authors` on both validator paths in `AC-1.3`, whereas the plan still specifies only four FR-1 fields across §\"Scope\", §\"Goals\" (G1), Stage 1, and §\"Deliverables\" and omits `AC-1.3` altogether.\n  class: build\n  quote: docs/01-plan/features/agy-coder-fallback.plan.md › Declare the four fields.\n  quote: docs/01-plan/features/agy-coder-fallback.spec.md › One entry per accepted implementation dispatch, so FR-7 §\"Attribution\" can recover a module's\n- Stage 7 (`FR-7`) and Stage 6 (`FR-10`) omit `implementation_authors` attribution recovery, the three closed unrecoverable-author-set cases, the SKILL.md Phase-5 `implementation_authors` step, and four of the five `AC-7.3` fixtures from Spec v1.8/v1.9 (`D-15`) — Spec FR-7 reads a module's author set from `implementation_authors` on every review leg, writes no entry when that set is unrecoverable (field absent, no entry for the module, or malformed), updates SKILL.md's Phase-5 orchestrator steps (FR-10), and pins five fixtures in `AC-7.3`, whereas Plan Stage 7 describes reading directly from the dispatch, carries only the single `implementer_switch.to=agy` fixture, and omits the FR-10 Phase-5 step.\n  class: build\n  quote: docs/01-plan/features/agy-coder-fallback.plan.md › implementation dispatch produced the code the leg reviews, read from that dispatch. It is\n  quote: docs/01-plan/features/agy-coder-fallback.spec.md › If the plan carries FR-1's field list or AC-7.3's fixtures, it gains\n- Stage 5 (`FR-5`) contradicts Spec FR-5 and `AC-5.2` on the wiring-check exit code for `AGY-GATE: UNREADABLE` (`1` vs `2`) and omits Spec v1.10's `--self-check` exit-0 verdict rule and `AC-5.2` fixture/mutant — Under \"Operational errors exit 2\", Stage 5 says `AGY-GATE: UNREADABLE` exits `1` from the check, contradicting Spec FR-5's table and `AC-5.2` which require the check to exit `2`; Stage 5 also omits Spec v1.10's rule that a `--self-check` `FAIL` verdict prints its token on stdout and exits `0` (including correcting the Codex gate's `FAIL shell-policy` branch) and its corresponding `AC-5.2` fixture and mutation check.\n  class: build\n  quote: docs/01-plan/features/agy-coder-fallback.plan.md › exits 1 from the check, and the\n  quote: docs/01-plan/features/agy-coder-fallback.spec.md › with exit 2, and the assembler\n  quote: docs/01-plan/features/agy-coder-fallback.spec.md › and so is one that returns 2 on a self-check\n- Stage 5 (`FR-4`, `FR-6`) and §\"Requirements\" omit Spec v1.8 and v1.10 (`D-16`) gate rules and `AC-4.1`/`AC-4.2` fixtures — The plan does not carry (1) FR-4's rule that every deny path ends `reason` with a closed-list `kind=\u003ckind\u003e` pinned per deny path in `AC-4.2`, (2) the two-layer activity scan where `_any_phase5_status(root) == \"unknown